2615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: todowrite]\n[tool: bash]\nDelegating the search test investigation to a subagent while I look at the rest.\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: task]\n[tool: todowrite]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: todowrite]\nThe whole suite now passes: `python3 -m unittest` ran 16 tests, all OK. The count went up from 15 because `tests/test_search.py` previously couldn't even load and was counted as a single error; now its 2 tests run. I didn't change any tests.\n\nI gave the `test_search.py` failure to a subagent to investigate. It also checked the other modules, and its findings matched my own reading of the code. There were six bugs, each fixed in `catalog/`:\n\n- **`search.py`**: it imported `normalize` from a module that doesn't exist (`catalog.nonexistent`). It now imports it from `catalog.text`.\n- **`members.py`**: the borrow limit `MAX_BORROWED` was set to 3, but the policy comment and the tests say 5. Changed to 5.\n- **`fees.py`**: the fee was days late *plus* 0.25 instead of days late *times* 0.25. Fixed to multiply.\n- **`inventory.py`**: `recent(n)` returned one event too many. It now returns exactly the last `n`. I also made it return an empty list when `n` is 0 or less, because the slice would otherwise return the whole history.\n- **`books.py`**: `parse_book` stored the year as text, which also broke `age()`. It now stores it as a whole number.\n- **`factory.py`**: `sample_books()` was missing the third book. I added `Book(\"Emma\", \"Austen\", 1815, 1)`. The tests only check the title \"Emma\", so I took the author, year and copies from the matching book in `test_search.py`.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "r